syntax:
Constructor definition outside the class body:

```c++
class MyClass {
public:
  MyClass(int x); // Constructor declaration
  // ... other members ...
};

MyClass::MyClass(int x) : member1(x), member2(x * 2) {  // Constructor definition
  // ... additional initialization if needed ...
}
```

**Note:**  The scope resolution operator `::` is crucial to associate the constructor definition with the class. The member initializer list (e.g., `member1(x), member2(x * 2)`) is preferred over assigning values within the constructor body for efficiency, particularly with complex objects.
